All this happens in the original game 
The original game subtracts moves if a move is made, then adds to moves if elements matched.
Then perfect gives additional single move, if perfect happenned in level where two types of elements
matched together, two addutional moves are given
Overall, moves remain unchanged if a unique element matches due to the move and only add up according to the "perfect" conditions
Using undo to achieve conditions of perfect do not work
